More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (761–770)
761. Improper Validation of Account Deletion Requests
Account Deletion Authorization Bypass
Attackers delete accounts belonging to other users due to missing authorization checks.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
762. Insecure Handling of API Key Permissions
API Key Privilege Escalation
API keys are assigned excessive permissions or can be modified by users.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
763. Improper Validation of Team Management APIs
Team Management Authorization Bypass
Attackers add themselves to restricted teams or organizations.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
764. Insecure Handling of Cloud Backup Storage
Cloud Backup Data Exposure
Cloud backup buckets are publicly accessible due to misconfiguration.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $12,000
765. Improper Validation of Activity Logs
Activity Log Information Disclosure
Activity logs reveal sensitive operations or user actions.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $5,000
766. Insecure Handling of Image Metadata
Image Metadata Leakage
Uploaded images reveal location data or internal system information through metadata.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
767. Improper Validation of User Tagging Systems
User Tagging Abuse
Attackers manipulate tagging systems to send spam or access restricted profiles.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
768. Insecure Handling of Real-Time Notification APIs
Real-Time Notification Exposure
Real-time notification systems leak user events or internal messages.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
769. Improper Validation of Device Management APIs
Device Management Authorization Bypass
Attackers manage or remove devices belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
770. Insecure Handling of User Activity Export
User Activity Data Exposure
Export features leak private user activity logs.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
